From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SnowBall Contributors <dev@snowballmc.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep chunk waits off world tick workers

The primary thread is at the world-tick barrier and cannot run a worker's
chunk dependencies. Reject such work before queueing it rather than letting
workers execute unrelated legacy or Moonrise tasks. The primary thread
keeps both normal queue drains. An idle worker can advance its world's
chunk ticket clock, but cannot process new tickets, unloads, or saves.

